## Scope note

*This section is informational. It does not modify the MIT grant above; it
clarifies which files in this repository the MIT grant is intended to apply
to, and which files carry a different license because they originate from a
third party.*

This repository contains two categories of material: **source code** (MIT)
and **data files** (CC-BY 4.0). It also references two **proprietary
hardware platforms** (Intel Loihi 2 and NVIDIA A100) and a set of
**third-party Python packages**, none of which are covered by the MIT
grant in this file. The subsections below state the category of each
file and directory in the repository.

### 1. Covered by the MIT grant

The MIT grant above applies to the following files and directories in
this repository.

| Path | Category | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `src/**` | Source code | Models, utilities, CLI tools, hardware simulators |
| `configs/**` | Configuration | All YAML configuration files |
| `scripts/**` | Source code | Training, evaluation, table and figure reproduction |
| `tests/**` | Source code | Unit tests, end-to-end tests, CLI replay tests |
| `expected_outputs/**` | Source code and metadata | Expected-output JSON and CSV, verification script, README |
| `data/*.py` | Source code | Dataset download, preprocessing, splitting, toy generator |
| `data/CHECKSUMS.txt` | Metadata | SHA-256 checksums; factual, not copyrightable |
| `data/README_data.md`, `data/README.md` | Documentation | Data documentation |
| `src/hardware_simulation/README_hardware.md` | Documentation | Hardware simulator documentation |
| `README.md`, `REPRODUCIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md` | Documentation | Top-level documentation |
| `requirements.txt`, `environment.yml` | Configuration | Pinned dependency list |
| `Dockerfile`, `setup.py`, `.gitignore` | Configuration | Build and packaging configuration |

**Attribution requirement.** Under the MIT grant, any copy or
substantial portion of the Software must include the copyright notice
and this permission notice. For a downstream research artifact, the
recommended attribution line is:

```
Portions of this work are derived from the PAFA-DoH Reproducibility
Artifact (Chapter 4 of the thesis), licensed under the MIT License.
```

The citation DOI for the underlying chapter is
`10.1016/j.neunet.2025.108343` (Neural Networks, April 2026).

### 2. Not covered — datasets (CC-BY 4.0)

The following data files are **not** covered by the MIT grant. They are
redistributed under, or are governed by, the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0) license, or are excluded from
this repository entirely.

| Dataset | License | Status in this repository |
|---|---|---|
| **Zenodo DoH corpus** — DOI [`10.5281/zenodo.5957677`](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5957677) (≈ 32 GB) | CC-BY 4.0 | **Not redistributed.** Fetched by `data/download_datasets.py` from the canonical DOI at runtime. |
| **CIC-DoH2023** — [`https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/dohbrw-2023.html`](https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/dohbrw-2023.html) (≈ 2.5 GB) | CC-BY 4.0 | **Not redistributed.** Fetched by `data/download_datasets.py` from the canonical URL at runtime. |
| **Toy dataset** — `data/toy_dataset/benign_sample.csv`, `data/toy_dataset/malicious_sample.csv` | CC-BY 4.0 | **Redistributed header-only.** The committed files contain only the 47-column schema header, no data rows. The full toy dataset is regenerated in place by `data/make_toy_dataset.py --mode synthetic --seed 42` and is a CC-BY 4.0 derivative of the Zenodo corpus. |
| **Generated outputs** — `outputs/**` | Depends on the generation command | Not committed. `outputs/tables/*.json` and `outputs/figures/*` reproduce Table 13–17 and Figures 7–10 of the chapter. If redistributed, they should carry the same MIT or CC-BY 4.0 status as the inputs they were generated from. |

Any downstream redistribution of the toy dataset, of generated
outputs derived from the Zenodo corpus or CIC-DoH2023, or of any
transformed version of those datasets must:

1. Preserve the CC-BY 4.0 attribution to the upstream dataset (a link
   to the DOI or URL is sufficient).
2. Preserve the CC-BY 4.0 notice alongside the data.
3. Not apply the MIT grant of this repository to those data files.
   The MIT grant is not a sublicense of the upstream data.

### 3. Not covered — proprietary hardware

The following hardware platforms are referenced by the artifact but
are **not** redistributed, emulated on bare metal, or sublicensed by
this repository.

| Hardware | Referenced in thesis | Status in this repository |
|---|---|---|
| **Intel Loihi 2** | §4.24.1 (128 neuromorphic cores × 1,024 LIF neurons = 128,000 neurons, 128 M synapses) | Proprietary Intel hardware. Not included, not emulated on bare metal. The reported 0.8 ms latency and 0.12 mJ / inference are reproduced by the calibrated software simulator `src/hardware_simulation/loihi_mock.py` within ±20 % / ±25 %, as documented in `REPRODUCIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md` §5. |
| **NVIDIA A100** | §4.24.1 (6,912 CUDA cores, 40 GB HBM; used as a comparison baseline in Table 13) | Proprietary NVIDIA hardware. Not included. The reported 2.1 ms latency and 1.8 mJ / inference are reproduced by `src/hardware_simulation/a100_emulation.py` within ±20 % / ±25 %. |
| **ChipWhisperer** | §4.26.3 (side-channel SNR measurement) | Proprietary NewAE Technology hardware. Not included. The SNN-guided noise injector is shipped (`src/models/ai_obfuscated_crypto.py`); the ChipWhisperer trace-acquisition step is not. |
| **IBM TrueNorth** | §4.24.1 — **mentioned only for comparison, not used in any reported experiment.** | Not included, not simulated, not measured. See `src/hardware_simulation/README_hardware.md` for the explicit non-use statement. |

The software simulators under `src/hardware_simulation/` are original
code, licensed under the MIT grant in this file. They emulate the
*reported numeric behaviour* of the hardware within the stated
tolerance; they do **not** emulate the hardware architecture, the
hardware instruction set, or any proprietary Intel, NVIDIA, NewAE or
IBM technology, and they do not imply any endorsement by those
vendors.

### 4. Not covered — third-party Python packages

This artifact depends on packages whose licenses are independent of
this file. The pinned list is in `requirements.txt` and
`environment.yml`. Each package retains its own upstream license,
which is available from the package's source repository or its PyPI
/ conda-forge listing. The principal dependencies and their typical
upstream license families are:

| Package | Typical upstream license | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `numpy`, `scipy`, `pandas`, `scikit-learn` | BSD-3-Clause | Numerical and data handling |
| `torch`, `torchvision`, `torchaudio` | BSD-3-Clause | Neural networks, federated training |
| `gudhi`, `ripser`, `persim` | MIT | Topological data analysis |
| `snntorch`, `brian2` | MIT / CeCILL-2.1 (brian2 upstream) | Spiking neural networks |
| `py_ecc` | MIT | BN128 pairing group for the Groth16 reference |
| `networkx` | BSD-3-Clause | Graph operations |
| `matplotlib`, `seaborn`, `graphviz` | PSF / BSD / EPL (graphviz binary) | Figure rendering |
| `PyYAML`, `requests`, `dask` | MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause | Configuration, download, parallel preprocessing |

The user is responsible for compliance with each upstream license.
This file does not relicense, sublicense, or extend those packages.

